  "problem": "The scalar curl of $F$ is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(-{y}^{3})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(3x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =0-(3x\\cdot 2y) \\\\  & =-6xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
